advertised metadata (the builtin table row)
-------------------------------------------

name          find_definition
description   "Find where a name is defined. Looks the name up in
              the prover's name spaces — constants, types, classes,
              facts, locales, methods, attributes — so it works for
              anything any command introduced (definition, fun,
              datatype, typedef, record, inductive, locale, ...).
              `kind` restricts the search (const | type | class |
              fact | locale | method | attribute); omitted searches
              all. Context: pass `repl` to search in that REPL's
              context, or `theory` for a loaded/image theory's global
              context; default is the base image. Each hit reports
              kind, full internal name, the definition position, and
              — when the defining theory has recorded segments or a
              loaded document — the complete defining source block
              (the whole datatype/fun/typedef command, showing
              constructors and fields the name space alone cannot)."
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {
                 "name": {"type": "string"},
                 "kind": {"type": "string",
                          "enum": ["const", "type", "class", "fact",
                                   "locale", "method", "attribute"]},
                 "repl": {"type": "string"},
                 "theory": {"type": "string"}},
               "required": ["name"]}
              (repl and theory are mutually exclusive — handler-
              enforced, like repl_init_from_source's locators.)
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": true, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}
outputSchema  none.

name/argument mapping across the layers
---------------------------------------

  mcp client edge   tools/call "find_definition",
                    {"name": "rev", "kind": "const"}
  scala builtin row backend.ir("find_definition", pairs of the given
                    args) after the exclusivity check.
  ml dispatcher     NEW entry: "find_definition" =>
                    (keys ["name", "kind", "repl", "theory"];
                     Ir_Nav.find_definition ...) — new ML code, lives
                    in MCP_Repl.thy (or a sibling Nav file in the
                    MCP-HOL session), NOT in ir/ir.ML (which stays
                    verbatim-reused; the Amazon-header constraint).
  engine (new ML)   resolve context: repl -> Toplevel.context_of of
                    its last state; theory -> Thy_Info.get_theory;
                    default -> the startup theory. spaces:
                    Sign.const_space, Sign.type_space, classes,
                    Proof_Context.facts_of, locales, methods,
                    attributes. per space: Name_Space.check /
                    extern-aware lookup of `name`, then
                    Name_Space.the_entry -> {theory_long_name, pos}.
                    enrich: pos + segments (Ir.find_source) ->
                    containing segment's text.

