open problem (2026-07-10): isabelle://theory/{name}/entities resource
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

spec's checklist bundles this resource into the SAME line as
find_definition/goto_definition ("navigation: find_definition ...,
goto_definition ..., isabelle://theory/{name}/entities resource"), but
no plan file owns it yet and it was never actually started -- this
note exists so the groundwork already done isn't lost before the tool
itself lands.

what it needs (spec, "concrete resources"): "entities *defined* in the
theory with kinds and positions -- consts, types (datatype/typedef/
type_synonym/record/...), classes, facts, locales -- from name-space
entries filtered by theory_long_name (image theories) or entity-def
markup in the snapshot (PIDE-loaded), replacing iq's regex-based
get_entities."

mechanism for the IMAGE-tier half, worked out but not yet written as
code: `Name_Space.theory_name {long = true} space name : string`
(Pure/General/name_space.ML) returns the defining theory's long name
for any entry directly -- no need to reconstruct it from positions or
markup. So, given `thy = Thy_Info.get_theory thy_name` and `target =
Context.theory_long_name thy`, the image-tier entities list is: for
each of

  Sign.class_space thy       -- classes
  Sign.type_space thy        -- types (datatype/typedef/type_synonym/
                                 record all land here per
                                 find_definition's own T2)
  Sign.const_space thy       -- consts
  Global_Theory.fact_space thy -- facts
  Locale.locale_space thy    -- locales

`Name_Space.get_names space` enumerated, filtered to entries where
`Name_Space.theory_name {long = true} space name = target`, with
position from `Name_Space.the_entry space name` (`#pos`, a
`Position.T`; `Position.line_of` for the line number). This is exactly
the name-space-enumeration counterpart to find_definition's per-space
lookup above (T1's kind coverage) -- if find_definition's Ir_Nav
module gets a per-space "list entries for theory X" helper, this
resource is a thin consumer of it; if find_definition doesn't need
one, this resource will have to add its own, following the same
pattern.

the PIDE-loaded (non-image) half is unexplored -- spec says "entity-
def markup in the snapshot", the same Rendering.entity_elements
cumulate goto_definition's plan already describes, just enumerating
instead of looking up one position; no mechanism verified yet for
that branch.

