update (2026-07-10, first implementation probed live): the resource
now exists (mcp_session.scala's theory_entities_uri -> MCP.ir fname
"entities" -> MCP_Repl.thy's entities function) and the heap-survival
assumption above is VERIFIED against a live `isabelle mcp_server -s
MCP-HOL`: isabelle://theory/HOL.Wellfounded/entities returns the real
kind/line/name table from a fresh process — Thy_Info.get_theory and
name-space entry positions DO survive heap restart; this is NOT the
segments gap.

ISSUE FOUND (name qualification): the scala gate and the ML lookup
accept DIFFERENT name forms. mcp_session.scala's image_tier tolerates
both spellings (loaded_theory(name) ||
loaded_theory(Long_Name.qualify(session_name, name))) but forwards
the client's ORIGINAL string to ML, where Thy_Info.get_theory does an
exact-key lookup against a table whose keys mix qualified and
unqualified names ("HOL.Wellfounded" but plain "Main"). live matrix
(mcp_server -s MCP-HOL -T MCP_Repl):

  MCP_Repl          gate passes, ML errors "Theory loader: undefined
                    entry for theory \"MCP_Repl\"" — the server's own
                    -T theory under its natural name fails
  MCP-HOL.MCP_Repl  ok (empty table — correct, ML-only theory)
  Main              ok
  HOL.Main          gate rejects -> misleading "not backed yet"
  Wellfounded       gate rejects -> misleading "not backed yet"
  HOL.Wellfounded   ok, real table

so the resource only answers for the exact Thy_Info key, which the
client cannot predict, and both failure modes mislead. fix direction:
have scala pass the RESOLVED qualified name (the form loaded_theory
actually matched) to ML, or have ML resolve base names against
Thy_Info.get_names before get_theory — either makes gate and lookup
agree by construction. the same latent mismatch sits in /commands and
bare /theory/{name}, masked there by the segments gap erroring first.
heap-behavior claims like the above are testable from scala via
MCP_Heap_Suite (see plans/README "testing process").

FIXED (2026-07-10, scala side): mcp_session.scala's image_theory
resolves the client spelling to the canonical loaded_theories key --
verbatim, then session-qualified, then a UNIQUE base-name match over
the whole image (unknown/ambiguous -> None, i.e. not image tier) --
and the RESOLVED name is what crosses the ir bridge, for entities and
for /commands + bare /theory/{name} alike (image_tier is now just
image_theory(name).isDefined; unload_theory's image check uses it
too). every row of the matrix above now answers: MCP_Repl,
Wellfounded and HOL.Main all resolve. pinned by the bridge test
"wave 2 resources: ... entities -- image-tier names are normalized to
the canonical Thy_Info key" (mcp_bridge_tests.scala).

